# The standalone viewer is served at an EXTENSIONLESS canonical URL, and
# BOTH rules below must stay ABOVE the splat: the SPA fallback matches
# everything, so a viewer request would otherwise be answered with the
# app shell — a page that cannot open a backup file and gives no hint why.
#
# The `.html` rule is not decoration. Cloudflare states that «redirects are
# always followed, regardless of whether or not an asset matches the incoming
# request», so the file sitting in `dist` does NOT shield that path from the
# splat: someone who typed the name they saw in a folder would be handed the
# app shell. One canonical URL, and everything else points at it.
#
# No loop: a 200 rewrite serves the asset at its destination, it does not
# re-enter this table. The live smoke checks that too, on every deploy.
/backup-viewer.html /backup-viewer 301
/backup-viewer /backup-viewer.html 200
/* /index.html 200
